 "template": "In this Odoo 17 app, create a new quotation (sales order) in the Sales app for the customer '{{v1}}'. Steps: open the Sales app, go to Orders > Quotations, click New. In the quotation form, set the Customer field to '{{v1}}' — it is an autocomplete dropdown, so type the name and actually select the matching option from the dropdown that appears (a value only counts when an option was chosen). Then in the Order Lines table, add ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (click into the product cell, type or search, and select an actual product option from the autocomplete dropdown), and set the quantity to 3. Let the app fill the unit price automatically. Do not wait for network idle (the app long-polls); wait for concrete page state. Then report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in for that line, and (c) the untaxed amount shown in the quotation's totals. Do NOT confirm the quotation yet — leave it as a draft quotation.",
